seg-6fe0d7cd4165 = <b>Compatibility contract.</b> Versions are <c1/>. New fields are added with <c2/> (the <em>additive discipline</em>), so a reader can parse any artifact of the <b>same major and an equal-or-older minor</b> (<c3/>). A strictly <b>newer minor</b> (<c4/>) may carry fields this reader cannot honour, and a <b>different major</b> (<c5/>) is a structural break — both are refused by <c6/>, which validates the format tag and version on the boundary rather than silently mis-parsing foreign input.

